      "name": "semantic_graph",
      "content": "{\"ok\": true, \"table_id\": \"SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"table_name\": \"SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"count\": 142, \"items\": [{\"metric_id\": \"dw_359\", \"name\": \"Yearly Math Lecture Units Above One Stddev with Undergraduate Majority\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year, what is the total number of lecture units for all subjects offered in regular terms by the Mathematics department (Course 18), where at least 60% of those subjects are undergraduate-level (HGN_DESC = 'Undergraduate'), considering only those academic years where the total lecture units are more than one standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) above the mean total lecture units across all academic years? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_1023\", \"name\": \"Math Fall Non-Variable Unit Statistics by Academic Year with Enrollment Filter\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Enrollment Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year where the Mathematics department has at least one unique subject with subject enrollment number greater than 10, what are the academic year, academic year description, department name, number of unique subjects, minimum total units offered, variance of total units, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of total units for subjects offered in the fall term that are not variable units and are offered by the Mathematics department? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_1049\", \"name\": \"Mathematics Total Units Stddev for Regular Non-Current Terms vs 2022 Degree-Granting Departments\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For the Mathematics department, what is the department name, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for its subjects in regular terms that are not the current term, and the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for subjects offered by that department in the 2022 academic year (considering only departments that have more than five subjects offered in 2022, are degree-granting, and are not the Chemistry department)? Show the department name, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) for regular non-current terms, and the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) for 2022. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_1973\", \"name\": \"Math 2022 Letter-Graded Subjects with TIP Materials Ranked by Term with 3-Row Max Units\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Textbook Material Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For all subjects offered in the academic year 2022 by the Mathematics department that have at least one associated TIP material and are also offered this year as letter graded, show the subject ID, subject title, term code, term description, the rank of each subject within its term (ordered by subject ID), subject code, subject number, department name, academic year, the maximum total units for each subject considering the current row and the next 2 rows ordered by subject code, and the start and end dates of the term. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_2090\", \"name\": \"Math 2024 12-Unit Subjects Ranked with Degree-Granting Undergraduate Course Count\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Course Catalog Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the academic year 2024 with a total of 12 units in the Mathematics department, show the subject code, subject number, subject title, department name, term description, and the rank of each subject within its department ordered by subject code, along with the department name, school name, the highest number of degree-granting undergraduate courses in the Mathematics department (Course 18), and the subject short title and subject description for each subject. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_2181\", \"name\": \"Chemistry Subjects with Course Materials 3-Row Max Enrollment vs Math Term Unit Statistics\", \"category\": \"Textbook Material and Enrollment Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each subject offered by the Chemistry department (Course 5) that has course materials, show the subject title, term code, offering department name, responsible faculty name, department full name, school name, the maximum number of enrolled students for each subject considering the current row and the next 2 rows ordered by subject offered key, along with the minimum academic year and average total units for the corresponding academic term in the Mathematics department, where the academic year is between 2000 and 2020 or the total units are at least 6, and the total units are between 1 and 12. Also, include the term description and the first day of classes for each term from the academic terms table. The results are ordered by term code and subject title. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_2461\", \"name\": \"Top 10 Chemistry Subjects by Enrollment with Prominent Faculty Department and Math Term Unit Statistics\", \"category\": \"Textbook Material and Enrollment Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"From the top 10 subjects offered by the Chemistry department (Course 5) with the highest number of enrolled students, display each subject's title, offering department name, responsible faculty name, term code, material status key, the maximum number of enrolled students for each subject considering the current row and the next 2 rows ordered by subject ID, and the department most represented among the responsible faculty for these subjects along with the count of subjects from that department. For each such subject, also provide the corresponding academic term parameter, the term description, the average total units, and the variance of total units of all subjects offered in the corresponding effective term, considering only subjects that are offered this year and are in the Mathematics department. The columns should be: subject title, offering department name, responsible faculty name, term code, material status key, maximum number of enrolled students, most prominent responsible faculty department, count of subjects from that department, academic term parameter, term description, average total units, and variance of total units. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_2580\", \"name\": \"Department Fall Non-Repeatable Subject Count Activity Classification by Year\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each department and academic year, provide the department name, academic year, the number of subjects offered that are not repeatable for credit and are offered in the fall term, and classify the department as 'HIGH_ACTIVITY' if it offers at least 10% more such subjects than the average across all departments for that year, 'LOW_ACTIVITY' if it offers at least 10% fewer, or 'AVERAGE' otherwise. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_2597\", \"name\": \"Department Average Total Units Deviation from Yearly Overall Average in Previous Terms\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year, what is the description of the academic year, the department name, the average total units for all subjects offered by that department in terms that match that academic year and have a term status indicator of 'P', and the deviation of each department's average total units from the overall average total units for that academic year? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_2628\", \"name\": \"Subject Group Max Enrollment and Average Total Units in Term 2019SP\", \"category\": \"Library Reserve and Enrollment Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each subject group in the term \\\"2019SP\\\", show the subject group ID and the highest number of enrolled students among all subjects in that group, along with the average total units for the group. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_2810\", \"name\": \"IAP Activities with Max Enrollment 12 by HASS Attribute with Rollup Totals\", \"category\": \"IAP Activity and Course Catalog Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For IAP subjects with a maximum enrollment of 12, show the activity title, enrollment type, academic year, term description, subject title, and the HASS attribute description. For each academic year, include a grand total for all HASS attribute descriptions in the format of (activity title, enrollment type, academic year, term description, null, total count). Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_2958\", \"name\": \"Non-Repeatable Subject Enrollment Average Variance Stddev by Department and Year\", \"category\": \"Enrollment Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year, among subjects that are not repeatable, what is the average, variance, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the number of enrolled students in subjects offered by each department? List the academic year, department name, average enrollment, variance, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP), ordered by variance descending. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3224\", \"name\": \"Union of 2010FA TIP Material Subjects and 2025FA Offered Subjects with Department Min Enrollment\", \"category\": \"Textbook Material and Enrollment Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"List all subjects from the term \\\"2010FA\\\" and all subjects offered in the term with code \\\"2025FA\\\", showing for each row: subject ID, term description, material status key, academic year, rank of the subject within each academic year group ordered by subject ID, subject title, offering department name, number of enrolled students, term start date, term end date, term parameter, the minimum number of enrolled students over each offering department, and the source term (\\\"2010FA\\\" or \\\"2025FA\\\"). The columns should appear in the following order: subject ID, term description, material status key, academic year, rank, subject title, offering department name, number of enrolled students, term start date, term end date, term parameter, minimum enrolled students per department, and source term. Order the results by subject ID and source term. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3248\", \"name\": \"2024 12-Unit Subjects Matched with Math Library Regular-Term Offerings and 3-Row Max Units\", \"category\": \"Library Reserve and Subject Offering Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the academic year 2024 with a total of 12 units that are also offered in the library by the Mathematics department during regular terms, show the subject code, subject number, subject title, department name, term description, the rank of each subject within its department ordered by subject code, the number of enrolled students, offering department name, academic year, subject short title, and the maximum total units for each row and the next two rows in order of subject ID. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3280\", \"name\": \"2019FA Subjects Dense Rank by Academic Year and School Running Sum of Total Units\", \"category\": \"Textbook Material and Enrollment Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the 2019FA term that have total units greater than 1, show the subject title, the dense rank of each subject considering the current and 2 preceding rows ordered by the academic year, the subject ID, the department name, and the running sum of total units within each school ordered by subject ID. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3294\", \"name\": \"Engineering Degree-Granting Courses Dense Rank by Budget Code with Current Term Running Year Sum\", \"category\": \"Course Catalog and Academic Term Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For courses in the School of Engineering that are degree granting, and for academic term parameters where the term indicator is 'C', show the course description, department name, the dense rank of each course considering the current and 2 preceding rows ordered by the department's budget code, the term parameter, the term code, the academic year, and the running sum of academic years within each department ordered by academic year, for cases where the department matches in both sets. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3357\", \"name\": \"Reserve Materials Status U Matched with Required Textbooks by Material Key and Year\", \"category\": \"Library Reserve and Textbook Material Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each library reserve material detail with material status key 'U', show the reserve catalog key, subject offered key, term code, academic year, term description, tip material key, tip material status key, and the average record count in a window of 2 preceding and 2 following rows grouped by the tip material status key and ordered by the academic year, along with the corresponding textbook material in the TIP_DETAIL table with material status key 'RQ' that matches on tip material key and academic year, showing the textbook subject offered key, textbook material key, subject ID, textbook academic year, textbook term description, and the row number within each textbook academic year group ordered by term code. Present the results in the order of reserve material academic year descending and textbook row number. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3393\", \"name\": \"2014FA Library Subjects with 5+ Enrolled Students by Material Status and Department Min Enrollment\", \"category\": \"Library Reserve and Enrollment Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For subjects with at least 5 enrolled students that are offered by the library in the term with code '2014FA', show the subject ID, subject title, number of enrolled students, term code, material status key, ISBN, row number within each material status group ordered by subject ID, offering department name, term description, term start date, term end date, and the minimum number of enrolled students for each offering department, ordered by offering department name, material status key, and subject ID. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3417\", \"name\": \"Previous Terms Windowed Academic Year Average with Regular-Term Unit Stddev by Year\", \"category\": \"Academic Term and Subject Offering Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each academic term where the term status indicator is 'P', show the term code, the term parameter, the term description, the academic year, the term start date, and the average academic year in a window of 2 preceding and 2 following rows grouped by the term indicator and ordered by the term start date. Additionally, for the academic year of each such term, give the academic year description, the average total units, and the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for subjects offered in regular terms, with the results ordered by term code and by the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of total units in descending order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3493\", \"name\": \"2022 12-Unit Subjects with Required or Optional Textbooks and Enrollment Windows\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Textbook Material Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the academic year 2022 with a total of 12 units that also have at least one required or optional textbook, show the subject code, subject number, department name, subject title, term description, total units, the average subject enrollment number in a window of 2 preceding and 2 following rows grouped by department code and ordered by total units, the textbook material key, the textbook material status key, and the row number of the course within each department ordered by subject code. List the results in order by department name, subject code, and subject number. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3530\", \"name\": \"2012SU Subjects Windowed Min Enrollment with Cross-Enrollment Total Units Stddev\", \"category\": \"Enrollment Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each subject offered in the term with code '2012SU', show the subject title, subject ID, offer department name, academic year, term description, the minimum number of enrolled students in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the academic year, and the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for that subject (considering only subjects offered by the \\\"Harvard Cross-Enrollment Prog\\\" department and with more than 5 offerings). Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3597\", \"name\": \"Cross-Term Subject Pairs 2019FA Enrollment Windows vs 2009SP Unit Row Numbers\", \"category\": \"Enrollment Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For all pairs of subjects where one is offered in the term '2019FA' with more than 0 enrolled students and the other is in the term '2009SP', show the 2019FA subject title, offer department name, department full name, number of enrolled students, and the average number of enrolled students in a window of 2 preceding and 2 following rows grouped by the school code, along with the 2009SP subject title, department name, total units, and the row number within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by subject title. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3612\", \"name\": \"IAP Activities Max Enrollment 30 with Required Textbook Record Count Windows\", \"category\": \"IAP Activity and Textbook Material Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For IAP subject activities with a maximum enrollment of 30 and tip details where the material status key is 'RQ', show the activity title, enrollment type, prerequisites, term code, IAP term description, term start date, term end date, the minimum term start date over each term code group, the tip subject offered key, tip material key, subject ID, tip term description, academic year, and the average record count in a window of 2 preceding and 2 following rows grouped by academic year, ordered by term code and academic year. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3632\", \"name\": \"2012SU Subject Enrollment Averages per Subject Key with Windowed Min Enrolled Students\", \"category\": \"Enrollment Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the term \\\"2012SU\\\", show the subject title, subject key, offer department name, subject enrollment number, subject offered summary key, the average subject enrollment number within each subject key group, subject ID, academic year, term description, and the minimum number of enrolled students in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row, ordered by offer department name and academic year. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3635\", \"name\": \"2024 12-Unit Subjects Matched with Same-Department 2019FA Offerings and Enrollment\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Enrollment Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the academic year 2024 with a total of 12 units, and for subjects offered in the term 2019FA from the same department, show the subject code, subject number, subject title, department name, term description, the rank of each 2024 subject within its department ordered by subject code, the 2019FA subject ID, number of enrolled students in 2019FA, department full name, and the row number of each 2019FA subject within its department name group ordered by subject ID. Order the results by department name, subject code, and 2019FA subject ID. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3660\", \"name\": \"Engineering Degree-Granting Courses with Fall 2024-2025 Subject Offerings Ranked per Department\", \"category\": \"Course Catalog and Textbook Material Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For courses in the School of Engineering that are degree granting, and for each subject offered in the term with the description \\\"Fall Term 2024-2025\\\" by the same department, show the course description, department name, the dense rank of each course considering the current and 2 preceding rows ordered by the department's budget code, the subject offered key, subject title, offering department name, the term description, and the rank of each subject within its offering department ordered by subject offered key. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3664\", \"name\": \"Top 10 Reserved-Material Subjects in 2009SP with Regular-Term Unit Average and Variance\", \"category\": \"Library Reserve and Subject Offering Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For the top 10 subject titles by the number of reserved library materials for subjects offered in the term '2009SP', display each subject title, the offering department name, the count of reserved materials, the academic year, the department name, the average of the total units, and the variance of the total units for subjects offered in regular terms, with the columns shown in that order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3727\", \"name\": \"Engineering Degree-Granting Departments 2021 Subject Counts and TIP Material Totals Union\", \"category\": \"Department Offering and Textbook Material Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each department that is degree-granting and offered at least one subject in the School of Engineering in 2021, or for each department that offered more than 10 tip materials for subjects in the School of Engineering during regular terms, provide the department code, department name, department full name, the number of subjects offered, the total number of enrolled students in those subjects, and the total number of tip materials. List the department code, department name, department full name, number of subjects offered, total number of enrolled students, and total number of tip materials in that order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3736\", \"name\": \"Subjects with Required Textbooks and Advance Sign-Up IAP Activities Max Enrollment 12\", \"category\": \"Library Reserve and IAP Activity Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each subject that both has a material status key of 'RQ' and also has an activity with enrollment type \\\"Advance sign-up required\\\" and a maximum enrollment of 12, show the subject title, the number of enrolled students from the RQ group, the term code from the library reserve material detail, the offer department name, the responsible faculty name, the tip material key, the row number within each tip material status key group ordered by subject title, the activity title, the term code from the IAP subject detail, the maximum enrollment, the term description, the term start date, the number of enrolled students from the IAP group, and the row number within each subject title group ordered by activity title. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3887\", \"name\": \"IAP Max Enrollment 12 Activities with Enrollment-Unit Difference and Department Subject Counts\", \"category\": \"IAP Activity and Course Catalog Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For IAP subjects with a maximum enrollment of 12, show the activity title, enrollment type, academic year, term description, subject title, the difference between the maximum enrollment and the total units, the subject code, subject code description, department name, and the number of subjects in the same department, for each subject offered in the same term and where the school code and subject title are not null. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3911\", \"name\": \"2014FA Library Subjects Enrollment Rollup by Department with Required Textbook Windowed Record Counts\", \"category\": \"Library Reserve and Enrollment Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each subject offered by the library in the term with code '2014FA', show the subject ID, subject title, total number of enrolled students, offering department name, term description, term start date, term end date, and the minimum number of enrolled students for each offering department, as well as the maximum windowed average record count from tip detail records with material status key 'RQ' (using a window of 2 preceding and 2 following rows grouped by financial aid year). Additionally, for each offering department, include a grand total row showing the total number of enrolled students across all its subjects (with nulls for subject ID and subject title), and the corresponding maximum windowed average record count if available. Order the results by offering department name and subject ID. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3944\", \"name\": \"2006FA Subjects and Engineering 1-Unit Subjects Lecture Unit Sums by Grade Type\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each subject that is both offered in the academic term with term code '2006FA' and is in the \\\"Engineering\\\" school with total units equal to 1, show the subject ID, subject title, department name, the sum of lecture units within each grade type group ordered by subject ID, the name of the responsible faculty member for each subject, the academic year, the rank of each subject within its academic year group ordered by subject ID, the term description, and the term start date, in that order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3959\", \"name\": \"2022FA Subjects Running Unit Sums Matched with Advance Sign-Up IAP Activities\", \"category\": \"IAP Activity and Subject Offering Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the term with code '2022FA' that also have at least one activity with an enrollment type of \\\"Advance sign-up required\\\" and a maximum enrollment of 12 (where the number of enrolled students is at least 10), show the subject ID, department name, subject term description, the running sum of total units within each academic year, subject title, whether the subject is offered in the fall term, the activity title, activity term code, activity maximum enrollment, activity term description, activity term start date, number of enrolled students in the activity, the offer department name for the activity, the responsible faculty name for the activity, and the row number of the activity within each subject title group, ordered by subject ID and activity title. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3985\", \"name\": \"2006FA Department Lecture Unit Sums with 2017JA Enrollment Classification per Subject Code\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Enrollment Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each subject offered in the academic term with term code '2006FA' in departments that offer more than 5 subjects in that term, show the subject ID, subject title, department name, the sum of lecture units within each grade type group, and the total number of subjects per department for that term. Additionally, for each subject offered by the same department in the term '2017JA', show the number of enrolled students, offering department name, department full name, subject code, subject code description, and whether the number of enrolled students is 'HIGH_ENROLLMENT' (at least 10% greater than the average for that subject code), 'LOW_ENROLLMENT' (at least 10% less than the average for that subject code), or 'AVERAGE'. Present the results ordered by subject ID and subject code. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3989\", \"name\": \"2024 Subjects Windowed Min Units with Engineering Course Description Length Deviation\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Course Catalog Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each department and each subject offered in the academic year 2024, show the department name, subject code, subject number, subject title, term code, term description, and the highest minimum total units (in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by academic year) for that subject, along with the course description, subject code description, and the difference between the number of characters in the course description and the average number of characters in course descriptions for that department, for courses in the School of Engineering that are degree granting. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_4019\", \"name\": \"2016SP Engineering School Subjects with Current Term Parameter Running Year Sums\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Course Catalog Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the term '2016SP' with a school code of 'E', show the subject title, department name, course description, the number of enrolled students, the row number within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by subject title, and the highest running sum of academic years (within that department) for academic term parameters where the term indicator is 'C'. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_4061\", \"name\": \"Department Geometric Mean Total Units with Academic Building Room Area Statistics\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Facility Space Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each department and academic year, show the department name, academic year, academic year description, and the geometric mean of the total units for all subjects offered by the department in regular terms with total units greater than zero, along with, for each academic building where these subjects are held and which has rooms larger than 40 square meters, the building name, the average, range, and variance of the room areas, as well as the total assignable area of the building and the year the building was built. The results are ordered by department name, academic year (descending), and room area range (descending). Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_4069\", \"name\": \"Advance Sign-Up IAP Activities Max Enrollment 12 Matched with Library Subjects 5+ Enrolled\", \"category\": \"IAP Activity and Library Reserve Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For subjects with an enrollment type of \\\"Advance sign-up required\\\" and a maximum enrollment of 12, and with at least 5 enrolled students, show the subject's activity title, term code, maximum enrollment, term description, term start date, subject title, number of enrolled students, the responsible faculty name, the row number within each subject title group ordered by activity title, the TIP material status key, the ISBN, and the row number within each material status group ordered by subject ID. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_4130\", \"name\": \"2012 Section-0 Cluster-S Subjects with Department Counts and Windowed Row Numbers\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the academic year 2012 that also have a section ID of 0 and a cluster type of 'S', show the subject key, subject title, offer department name, academic year, term description, the total number of subjects offered by each department in that year, the row number within each offer department name group ordered by subject key, the department name from SUBJECT_SUMMARY, the term start date from ACADEMIC_TERMS, and the row number within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by the subject title from SUBJECT_OFFERED. List the results in order by offer department name and subject key. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_4305\", \"name\": \"Top 10 Fall 2024-2025 Enrolled Subjects in Departments with Above-Average 2022SU Units\", \"category\": \"Enrollment Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For the top 10 subjects offered in the term with the description \\\"Fall Term 2024-2025\\\" that have the highest number of enrolled students, display each subject's offered key, subject title, offering department name, the term description, the number of enrolled students, and the rank of each subject within its offering department (ordered by subject offered key), but only include subjects where the offering department is among those that, in the term with code '2022SU', had an average total units for their subjects greater than the average total units for all subjects offered in that term. List the subject offered key, subject title, offering department name, term description, number of enrolled students, and the rank within the department, in that order, and order the results by department name and number of enrolled students descending. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_4308\", \"name\": \"2017JA Subjects Enrollment per Subject Code with 2019FA School Running Unit Sums\", \"category\": \"Enrollment and Subject Offering Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the term '2017JA', show the subject title, number of enrolled students, offering department name, department full name, subject code, subject code description, and the minimum number of enrolled students over each subject code group, as well as the school code, school name, department code, school name from department, department phone number, and the highest running sum of total units for any subject within that school in the 2019FA term (where the subject has more than 1 total unit). Order the results by subject code. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_4387\", \"name\": \"Engineering Departments Above-Average Enrollment with Highest Regular-Term Average Units\", \"category\": \"Enrollment and Subject Offering Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each department in the School of Engineering with total student enrollment in its courses greater than the average total enrollment across all Engineering departments (and with total enrollment greater than 50), display the department name, the total number of students enrolled in its courses, and the highest average total units for subjects it has ever offered in a regular academic term, listing the results in descending order of total enrollment. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_4448\", \"name\": \"Department Highest 12-Unit Fall 2024-2025 Subjects with 2022 Above-Average Textbook Courses\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Textbook Material Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each department, show the department name, the highest total units among its subjects with exactly 12 units in the Fall Term 2024-2025, and for each course in that department that was offered in 2022 and has at least one required or optional textbook and has total units greater than the average for such courses, show the course's subject code, subject number, subject title, the term description, the textbook material key, the textbook material status key, and the row number within the department ordered by subject code. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_4473\", \"name\": \"Engineering 6+ Unit Subjects Grade-Type Running Unit Sums with IAP Activity Rollup Counts\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and IAP Activity Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered by departments in the School of Engineering with a total of at least 6 units, show the subject code, subject title, department name, grade type, and the running sum of total units within each grade type, but only include those subjects where the running sum exceeds 12 units within their grade type. For each such subject, also show, for IAP subject activities with a maximum enrollment of at least 10 and that are not cancelled and are associated with the same subject code, the academic term description, activity title, enrollment type, and the total count of such activities (with a grand total row for all activities in each term, where activity title, enrollment type, and subject title are null and the total count is for all activities in that term). Order the results by subject code, academic term description, and activity title. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_4515\", \"name\": \"Department Year Subject Statistics Matched with IAP Activity Sponsor Statistics\", \"category\": \"IAP Activity and Subject Offering Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each department, academic year, activity title, and sponsor name where the subject enrollment number is greater than 10 and the maximum enrollment for the activity is greater than 10, provide the department name, academic year, number of unique subjects, minimum total units offered, activity title, sponsor name, number of unique activities, minimum fee, and the sponsor type. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_4558\", \"name\": \"Required Textbook Record Count Windows Matched with Non-Cancelled IAP Activities\", \"category\": \"Textbook Material and IAP Activity Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For tip details where the material status key is 'RQ' and for IAP subject activities that are not cancelled and have a maximum enrollment greater than 10, show the tip subject offered key, material key, subject ID, term description, academic year, the average record count in a window of 2 preceding and 2 following rows grouped by academic year (as tip_window_avg_record_count), the activity title, enrollment type, maximum enrollment, academic term description from the time day table, term start date from the academic terms table, the minimum maximum enrollment value over each term code group (as iap_min_max_enrollment), and the academic year description from the academic terms table, ordered by academic year and IAP term code. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_4566\", \"name\": \"Fall 2024-2025 Subjects with Status-U Library Reserve Materials Ranked per Department\", \"category\": \"Library Reserve and Enrollment Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each subject offered in the term with the description \\\"Fall Term 2024-2025\\\" that also has more than 0 enrolled students and a material status key of 'U', show the subject offered key, subject title, offering department name, the term description, the rank of each subject within its offering department, the course number, course number description, number of enrolled students, the reserve catalog key, the dense rank over the material status key, and the academic year description, ordered by subject offered key and course number. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_4583\", \"name\": \"Status-U Reserve Materials Record Count Windows with Catalog Record Counter Statistics\", \"category\": \"Library Reserve and Textbook Material Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each library reserve material detail with material status key 'U', show the reserve catalog key, subject offered key, term code, the academic year, the term description, the tip material key, the tip material status key, and the average record count in a window of 2 preceding and 2 following rows grouped by the tip material status key and ordered by the academic year, along with the average and variance of the record counter for reserve catalog items associated with that material status key where the catalog year is greater than 2000. Additionally, for each result, include the catalog title and catalog author name from the reserve catalog. Present the results ordered by academic year descending and record counter variance descending. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_4584\", \"name\": \"Mathematics Library Subjects Above Yearly Average Enrollment in Previous Terms\", \"category\": \"Library Reserve and Enrollment Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For Mathematics department courses with at least 5 enrolled students, show the course number, subject title, number of enrolled students, term description, academic year, the row number within each academic year group ordered by course number, the term start date, calendar date, day of week, and the average calendar year within each calendar year group ordered by term start date, but only for academic terms where the term status is 'Previous', and only include results where the number of enrolled students is greater than the average number of enrolled students for that academic year. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_4650\", \"name\": \"Engineering Degree-Granting Departments 2021 Enrollment per Subject and per TIP Material Ratios\", \"category\": \"Department Offering and Textbook Material Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each degree-granting department that offered at least one subject in the School of Engineering in 2021 and has more than 10 tip materials for subjects in the School of Engineering during regular terms, provide the department code, department name, department full name, the number of subjects offered, the total number of enrolled students in those subjects, the total number of tip materials, the average number of enrolled students per subject (rounded to two decimal places), and the ratio of total enrolled students to total tip materials (rounded to two decimal places), listing the results in descending order of the average number of enrolled students per subject.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_4658\", \"name\": \"Mathematics Library Subjects 5+ Enrolled in Previous Terms with Faculty and Calendar Attributes\", \"category\": \"Library Reserve and Enrollment Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"Show the Mathematics department courses with at least 5 enrolled students, including the course number, subject title, number of enrolled students, term description, academic year, the row number within each academic year group ordered by course number, the term start date, calendar date, day of week, the average calendar year within each calendar year group ordered by term start date, and for each course, also display the responsible faculty name and the offer school name, but only for academic terms where the term status is 'Previous'. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_4683\", \"name\": \"Current Term Department Enrollments with Library Course Counts and Min Units\", \"category\": \"Library Reserve and Enrollment Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each department where the total number of subject enrollments for subjects offered in the current term is greater than 10, and for each course number in that department where the number of enrolled students in the subject summary is greater than 2, provide the department name, the total number of subject enrollments, the course number, the number of unique library subjects offered, the minimum total units for those subjects, and the name of the responsible faculty member for each course. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_4701\", \"name\": \"Yearly Geometric Mean Reserve Materials per Subject with Fall Term Unit Statistics\", \"category\": \"Library Reserve and Subject Offering Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year, what is the academic year, academic year description, the geometric mean of the number of library reserve material details per subject offered (considering only records where the material status is 'U' and the academic term is a regular term), the average total units, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of total units, and the average number of design units for subjects that are offered in the fall term and have a material status of 'U' in the library reserve? List the results ordered by the geometric mean of materials per subject in descending order, then by the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of total units in descending order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_4724\", \"name\": \"Mathematics Library Regular-Term Subjects 3-Row Max Units with Required Material Department Statistics\", \"category\": \"Library Reserve and Textbook Material Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each subject offered in the library in the Mathematics department during regular terms, show the subject title, number of enrolled students, offering department name, term description, academic year, subject short title, and the maximum total units for each row and the next two rows in order of subject ID. Additionally, for the corresponding offering department and school, provide the number of unique subjects with course material status 'RQ' and the minimum total units for those subjects. Also, include the department phone number and the school name for the offering department, and display the responsible faculty name for each subject. The columns should be shown in the following order: subject title, number of enrolled students, offering department name, term description, academic year, subject short title, maximum total units for each row and the next two rows, number of unique subjects with course material status 'RQ', minimum total units for those subjects, department phone number, school name, and responsible faculty name. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_4756\", \"name\": \"Department Course Counts with 2022 12-Unit Subjects Having Textbooks\", \"category\": \"Course Catalog and Department Analysis\", \"desc\": \"Show the department names, the corresponding SIS subject code, subject code descriptions, graduate level, the total number of courses per department, and for each department, the number of subjects offered in the academic year 2022 with a total of 12 units that also have at least one required or optional textbook. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_4826\", \"name\": \"Status-U Reserve Materials Windowed Year and Record Count Statistics with Normalized Ratio\", \"category\": \"Library Reserve and Textbook Material Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each library reserve material with material status key 'U', list the subject ID, library course instructor key, term description, academic year, term start date, the minimum academic year in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by library reserve catalog key, the library subject offered key, the tip material key, the tip material status key, the average record count in a window of 2 preceding and 2 following rows grouped by the tip material status key and ordered by the academic year, and for each, include the academic year description and the last day of final exam from the ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL table, and calculate the normalized year to average record count ratio (academic year divided by average record count in the window), ordered by the normalized year to average record count ratio descending.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_4978\", \"name\": \"Status-U Reserve Materials Matched with Required Textbooks Including Term Start and End Dates\", \"category\": \"Library Reserve and Textbook Material Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each library reserve material detail with material status key 'U', show the reserve catalog key, subject offered key, term code, academic year, term description, tip material key, tip material status key, and the average record count in a window of 2 preceding and 2 following rows grouped by the tip material status key and ordered by the academic year, along with the corresponding textbook material in the TIP_DETAIL table with material status key 'RQ' that matches on tip material key and academic year, showing the textbook subject offered key, textbook material key, subject ID, textbook academic year, textbook term description, and the row number within each textbook academic year group ordered by term code. Additionally, for each matching textbook material, include the term start date and term end date from the ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL table. Present the results in the order of reserve material academic year descending and textbook row number. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_41\", \"name\": \"Yearly Average and Variance of Math Full-Term Subject Total Units in Previous Terms\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year, provide the academic year description and calculate the average and variance of the total units for subjects offered in terms that are not the current term, have a term status indicator of 'P', are offered by the Mathematics department, and are full term subjects. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_1288\", \"name\": \"Math IAP Max Enrollment Variance Rollup with Library and TIP Department Enrollment Totals\", \"category\": \"Library Reserve and IAP Activity Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year, what is the variance and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the maximum enrollment for IAP activities offered in that year by the Mathematics department, considering only activities that require advance sign-up and are not cancelled, and also provide the academic year description? For each department, include a grand total for all activities in the format of (department name, null, total variance and stddev). Additionally, for each such department, provide the department code, the department name, and the total number of enrolled students in both the library and tip subject offerings, but only for those departments where the total number of enrolled students is more than one standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) above the mean total enrolled students across all departments, and restrict your answer to departments whose name is 'Mathematics' (Course 18). Also, for each such department, list the names of the responsible faculty members from both the library and tip subject offerings. The columns to display, in order, are: department name, academic year description, total variance, total standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP), department code, department name, total enrolled, library faculty, and tip faculty. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_1301\", \"name\": \"Math Yearly Max Total Units with Fall-Term Library Enrollment Stddev and Equivalent Subjects\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Enrollment Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year, where the maximum number of total units for any Mathematics (Course 18) subject offered in that year is greater than 9 and there are more than 5 Mathematics subjects offered in the fall term, what are the academic year, the maximum total units, the corresponding term description, the subject title, the academic year description, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the number of enrolled students in library subjects offered during terms in that year, and the average number of equivalent subjects for those library subjects? List the results in order of academic year. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_1393\", \"name\": \"Math Current-Term Unit Dispersion with Degree-Granting Department Course Counts\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Course Catalog Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year and department in Mathematics, what is the variance and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for subjects offered in that year and department (considering only subjects offered in the current term, with more than 0 total units, and with subject enrollment number greater than the average for that department and year), and for those departments, what are the department code, corresponding administrative department name, the graduate level of courses, and the total number of distinct courses per department, for all degree-granting departments except the Management department? Present the results as academic year, department name, total units variance, total units standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP), department code, administrative department name, graduate level, and number of distinct courses, in that order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_1427\", \"name\": \"Math Graduate Degree-Granting Courses Ranked by Admin Department with Spring 2021 Letter-Graded Unit Summary\", \"category\": \"Course Catalog and Department Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each course in the Mathematics department that is degree granting and has a course level of 'G', show the course description, department name, school name, the administrative department name, and the dense rank over the administrative department name ordered by the administrative department name. Additionally, for each administrative department name, include a grand total of the number of such courses in the format of (null, null, null, administrative department name, null, total courses). Also, show the minimum total units, the sum of lecture units, and the number of unique subjects for letter graded Mathematics department subjects offered in the Spring Term 2021, along with the department name and term description (with all other columns as null). Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_1618\", \"name\": \"School CIP Categories with Yearly Math IAP Max Enrollment Stddev and Department Phone\", \"category\": \"IAP Activity and Course Catalog Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each school, what is the school's name, the school's name in the commencement book, the maximum CIP program code among its degree-granting departments' courses (excluding the Mathematics department), the CIP category ('HIGH_CIP', 'LOW_CIP', or 'MEDIUM_CIP'), the academic year, the academic year description, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the maximum enrollment for IAP activities offered by the Mathematics department in that year (considering only years with more than five activities), and the Mathematics department phone number, for schools where the maximum CIP program code is greater than 130000 and the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of maximum enrollment is available? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_1692\", \"name\": \"Math Degree-Granting Course Levels Above Average Enrollment with Spring 2021 Letter-Graded Summary\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Enrollment Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each department name and course level in the Mathematics department (Course 18) where the total number of enrolled students in offered subjects is greater than the average number of enrolled students for that department and the subjects are degree-granting, provide the number of unique courses and the minimum total units among those subjects, along with the term description, the minimum total units, the sum of lecture units, and the number of unique subjects for letter graded Mathematics subjects offered in the Spring Term 2021. List the columns in the following order: department name, course level, number of unique courses, minimum total units from the first set, term description, minimum total units from the second set, sum of lecture units, and number of unique subjects. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_2180\", \"name\": \"2014FA Chemistry Library Subjects Windowed Enrollment with Math Unit Coefficient of Variation and Required Material Counts\", \"category\": \"Library Reserve and Textbook Material Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the term '2014FA' by the Chemistry department, show the subject title from the library, the number of enrolled students in the library subject, the responsible faculty name from the TIP subject, the offer department name from the TIP subject, the minimum number of enrolled students in the library subject within a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the TIP subject's responsible faculty MIT ID, and for each academic year, also show the academic year and academic year description and the coefficient of variation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for subjects in the Mathematics department (Course 18) that have more than 0 total units and are offered in terms with a term status indicator of 'P'. Additionally, for each Chemistry subject, include the number of required TIP materials (where TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY = 'RQ') for that subject in that term. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_2560\", \"name\": \"Chemistry Subjects with Course Materials 3-Row Max Enrollment vs Math Term Unit Statistics with Final Exam Date\", \"category\": \"Textbook Material and Enrollment Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each subject offered by the Chemistry department (Course 5) that has course materials, provide the subject title, term code, offering department name, responsible faculty name, department full name, school name, and the maximum number of enrolled students for each subject considering the current row and the next 2 rows ordered by subject offered key, along with the minimum academic year and average total units for the corresponding academic term in the Mathematics department, where the academic year is between 2000 and 2020 or the total units are at least 6, and the total units are between 1 and 12. Additionally, include the term description and the last day of final exam for each term from the academic terms table. The results should be listed in order by term code and subject title. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3215\", \"name\": \"2012 Subjects Department Row Numbers with Subject Code School Dense Ranks\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Course Catalog Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the academic year 2012, show the subject key, subject title, offer department name, academic year, term description, the row number within each offer department name group ordered by subject key, the subject code, subject code description, department name, and the dense rank of each row partitioned by the school code and ordered by school code, for subjects where the school code is not null and the subject title is not null. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3268\", \"name\": \"Union of 2025FA Offered Subjects and Engineering 6+ Unit Subjects with Running Unit Sums\", \"category\": \"Textbook Material and Enrollment Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"List all subjects that are either offered in the term with code '2025FA' or are offered by departments in the School of Engineering with a total of at least 6 units. For each subject, show the subject ID, subject title, department name, number of enrolled students, term description, academic year, term start date, term end date, term parameter, the minimum number of enrolled students over each offering department, the running sum of total units within each school, and the reason for inclusion ('2025FA Subjects' for subjects offered in the term '2025FA' and 'Engineering 6+ Units' for subjects offered by Engineering departments with at least 6 units), ordered by subject ID. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3277\", \"name\": \"Union of 2022FA 12-Unit Subjects Dense Rank and Master Section 3-Row Max Enrollment\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Enrollment Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"List all subject titles that are either (a) offered in the term '2022FA' with a total of 12 units, showing the subject title, department name from the course description, and the dense rank of each subject considering the current and 2 preceding rows ordered by the subject code from the course catalog, or (b) for each subject offered, show the subject title, subject ID, offer department name, offer school name, term description, academic year, and the maximum number of enrolled students for each subject considering the current row and the next 2 rows ordered by subject key. The results should include all these columns in the following order: subject title, department name, window column, offer department name, offer school name, term description, academic year, and maximum number of enrolled students, with NULLs for columns not relevant to each case. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3398\", \"name\": \"Required-Textbook Subjects Ranked per Department Matched with Master Section 3-Row Max Enrollment\", \"category\": \"Textbook Material and Enrollment Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each subject offered in the same term as a TIP detail record with material status 'RQ', show the subject key, subject title, offer department name, TIP material key, and the rank of each record within each offer department name group ordered by subject key, along with the subject title, subject ID, offer department name, offer school name, term description, academic year, and the maximum number of enrolled students for each subject considering the current row and the next 2 rows ordered by subject key, where the subject, term, and offer department name match in both cases. List the columns in the following order: subject key, subject title, offer department name, TIP material key, rank, subject title (from the second subquery), subject ID, offer department name (from the second subquery), offer school name, term description, academic year, and the maximum number of enrolled students. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3436\", \"name\": \"Union of Library Subjects 5+ Enrolled and IAP Activities Max Enrollment 12\", \"category\": \"Library Reserve and IAP Activity Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"List all subjects with at least 5 enrolled students, showing the subject ID, subject title, number of enrolled students, term code, material status key, ISBN, and the row number within each material status group ordered by subject ID, as well as all IAP subject activities with a maximum enrollment of 12, showing the subject ID, activity title, enrollment type, term description, and the rank of each record within each term description group ordered by activity title. Indicate the source of each record as either 'LibrarySubject' or 'IAPActivity'. The columns should be: subject ID, subject title, number of enrolled students, term code, material status key, ISBN, window column, activity title, enrollment type, term description, and source. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3498\", \"name\": \"Union of 2025FA Offered Subjects and 2016SP Degree-Granting Department Subjects with Unit Dense Ranks\", \"category\": \"Textbook Material and Enrollment Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"List all subject IDs that are either offered in the term with code '2025FA' or are offered in the term '2016SP' by departments that grant degrees, along with the subject title, offering department name, number of enrolled students, term description, academic year, term start date, term end date, term parameter, the minimum number of enrolled students over each offering department, and the dense rank considering the current and 2 preceding rows ordered by the total number of units. For subjects from the term '2025FA', show the subject title, offering department name, number of enrolled students, term description, academic year, term start date, term end date, term parameter, and the minimum number of enrolled students over each offering department; for subjects from the term '2016SP' by degree-granting departments, show the dense rank as window_column. The results are ordered by subject ID. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3684\", \"name\": \"2025FA Engineering Subjects Enrollment Windows with Catalog Unit Row Numbers\", \"category\": \"Textbook Material and Enrollment Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the term with code '2025FA' by departments in the School of Engineering, show the subject ID, subject title, offering department name, number of enrolled students, term description, academic year, term start date, term end date, term parameter, the minimum number of enrolled students over each offering department, total units, department full name, and assign row numbers within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by subject title, ordered by offering department name and subject title. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3861\", \"name\": \"2017FA High-Unit Subjects Dense Rank Matched with 2022SU Unit Dense Ranks\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Course Catalog Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For subject offerings in the term '2017FA' with a total number of units greater than 10, display the subject title, department name, school name, and their dense rank considering the current and 2 preceding rows ordered by the department code from the subject code table, along with any matching subject IDs from subjects offered in the term with code '2022SU', their department names, and their dense rank considering the current and 2 preceding rows ordered by the total number of units. Show the subject title, department name, school name, subq1 dense rank, subject ID, subq2 department name, and subq2 dense rank, in that order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3867\", \"name\": \"Subject Code Department Counts Matched with 2022FA Above-Average Unit Running Sums\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Course Catalog Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each subject in a department where the school code and subject title are not null, and for each subject offered in the 2022FA term with total units greater than the average for that term, display the subject code, subject code description, department name, subject title, the number of subjects in the same department, the subject ID, the term description, and the running sum of total units for that academic year, ordered by subject ID. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3904\", \"name\": \"Degree-Granting Subject Code Description Status Rollup by School with 2022SU Unit Dense Ranks\", \"category\": \"Course Catalog and Department Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each subject code where the department is degree granting, show the subject code, subject code description, department name (from subject code), school name, the number of subject codes per school name and whether the subject code description is present ('Has Description') or missing ('No Description'), and for each matching department in subjects offered in the term with code '2022SU', show the subject's ID, total units, department name (from subject offered), and their dense rank considering the current and 2 preceding rows ordered by the total number of units. For each school name, include a grand total for all subject codes in the format of (null, null, null, school name, null, total subject codes, null, null, null, null). Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3973\", \"name\": \"ISBN-Sourced Textbook Material Prices with Non-Current Term Enrollment Deviations\", \"category\": \"Textbook Material and Enrollment Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"List the term code, subject ID, minimum record count from TIP_DETAIL, total new shelf price from TIP_MATERIAL, academic year, number of enrolled students, and deviation from the average number of enrolled students for that academic year, for each term and subject where the material has a non-null author and a material info source of 'ISBN', and considering only terms that are not the current term. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_4184\", \"name\": \"2012 Department Subject Counts with 2012SU Enrollment Averages and Deviations per Subject Key\", \"category\": \"Enrollment Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each department, show the offer department name, the number of distinct subjects offered by the department in the academic year 2012, and for each subject that was offered in the term \\\"2012SU\\\", display the subject key, subject title, academic year, term description, subject enrollment number, subject offered summary key, the average subject enrollment number within each subject key group, and the deviation of each subject's enrollment number from the average enrollment number for its subject key group, ordered by offer department name and subject key. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_4197\", \"name\": \"2012SU Cluster-S Subjects Enrollment Deviations from Department Averages with Dense Ranks\", \"category\": \"Enrollment Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each subject offered in the term with term code '2012SU' that also has a cluster type of 'S', show the subject title, offer department name, offer school name, cluster type description, the difference between the number of enrolled students for that subject and the average number of enrolled students for all subjects in the same department in that term, the dense rank of each subject considering the current and 2 preceding rows ordered by the number of enrolled students, and the deviation of the number of enrolled students from the average number of enrolled students for that department in that term as calculated from the summary table. The columns should be shown in the following order: subject title, offer department name, offer school name, cluster type description, deviation from department average (from the first calculation), window column (dense rank), and deviation from department average (from the summary calculation). Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_4229\", \"name\": \"Mathematics IAP Category Activities Matched with Fall-Term Department Enrollment Statistics\", \"category\": \"IAP Activity and Subject Offering Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For IAP subjects in the \\\"Mathematics\\\" category, show the activity title, enrollment type, maximum enrollment, category name, activity description, and the row number within each enrollment type group ordered by activity title, along with the academic year, department name, average enrollment, enrollment variance, department phone number, and school name for each academic year and department where the IAP subject's term matches a department's fall term subject offering with more than 0 enrolled students. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_4231\", \"name\": \"Current SIS Term Department Subjects Matched with 2016SP Degree-Granting Department Unit Totals\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Textbook Material Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each department that both offered subjects in the current SIS term and is a degree-granting department that offered subjects in the term '2016SP', list the department code, offering department name, subject title, responsible faculty name, term description, academic year description, total number of subjects offered per department in the current term, department name, number of subjects offered in 2016SP, and total units for those subjects in 2016SP. Include all columns in the order: department code, offering department name, subject title, responsible faculty name, term description, academic year description, total number of subjects offered per department in the current term, department name, number of subjects offered in 2016SP, and total units for those subjects in 2016SP. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_4287\", \"name\": \"Status-U Reserve Materials Above-Average Enrollment Matched with 2025FA Subject Attributes\", \"category\": \"Library Reserve and Textbook Material Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each library reserve material detail with material status key equal to 'U' and for subjects offered in the term with code '2025FA', show the library course instructor key, library reserve catalog key, term code, subject ID, the tip material key, tip material status key, tip ISBN, the subject title from the subject offered table, the minimum tip material status key in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the number of enrolled students (only including those where the number of enrolled students is greater than the average across all subjects), the offering department name, term description, academic year, term start date, term end date, term parameter, the minimum number of enrolled students over each offering department, the offering school name, and the responsible faculty name for each subject. Order the results by offering department and descending number of enrolled students. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_4405\", \"name\": \"IAP Activity Category Ranks Cross-Joined with Department Year Enrollment Statistics\", \"category\": \"IAP Activity and Subject Offering Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each combination of activity and department/academic year enrollment statistics, list the activity title, enrollment type, maximum enrollment, category name, category description, and the dense rank of each row partitioned by the category name and ordered by the category name, along with the department name, academic year, number of unique subjects offered (subject count), minimum number of total units for those subjects, and the average number of enrolled students per subject (for departments and academic years where the number of enrolled students in a subject is greater than 5). Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_4738\", \"name\": \"Union of Fall 2024-2025 Offered Subjects Ranked per Department and Required Textbook Record Count Windows\", \"category\": \"Textbook Material and Enrollment Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each subject offered in the term with the description \\\"Fall Term 2024-2025\\\", show the subject ID, subject title, offering department name, term description, and the rank of the subject within its offering department. For each tip detail record where the material status key is 'RQ', show the subject ID, term description, term start date, tip material key, and the average record count in a window of 2 preceding and 2 following rows grouped by the financial aid year. Additionally, for each subject offered in \\\"Fall Term 2024-2025\\\", include the academic year description from the academic terms table. Indicate the source of each row as either 'SubjectOffered' or 'TipDetail'. The results should be ordered by subject ID and source. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_4911\", \"name\": \"Top 10 Engineering Subjects by 3-Row Max Enrollment with Catalog Unit Row Numbers\", \"category\": \"Enrollment Analysis\", \"desc\": \"From the top 10 subjects offered by departments in the School of Engineering with the highest maximum enrolled students (considering the current and next 2 rows ordered by subject key), display each subject's title, total units, department full name, row number within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by subject title, subject ID, offer department name, offer school name, term description, academic year, and the department that offered the subject. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_5103\", \"name\": \"2017JA TIP Subjects Enrollment Windows Matched with 2022FA Catalog Running Unit Sums per Department\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Textbook Material Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the term '2017JA', show the subject title, the number of enrolled students, the responsible faculty name, the offering department name, the department full name, the school name, and the minimum number of enrolled students in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the department code. Additionally, for subjects offered in the term with code '2022FA' in the same department, provide the subject ID, department name, term description, the running sum of total units within each academic year ordered by subject ID, and the subject's short title and responsible faculty name from the course catalog. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3901\", \"name\": \"2012SU Subject Offerings Dense Rank Matched with Department-6 CIP Course Classification and School Rollups\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and CIP Program Classification Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each offer department code in the 2012SU term with total units greater than 0, list the subject title, course number, department name, the dense rank over the offer department code, the course, course description, school name, program code, program title, category code, category title, four digit code, four digit title, and the minimum warehouse load date from the CIP table over each category code group for courses in department 6, and include a grand total of subjects per offer department code and a grand total for all courses in each school in the format (nulls for subject-specific fields, department name, total subjects, course-specific fields, school name, and total courses). Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_50\", \"name\": \"2021 Non-Graduate-Credit Math Undergraduate Catalog Subjects Offered by Science School Count\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Course Catalog Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"How many subjects offered in 2021 that are not for graduate credit, are listed as undergraduate in the course catalog, are in the Mathematics department, and are also offered by the School of Science? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_1335\", \"name\": \"Union of Math 2008 Unit Range-Variance with Long Descriptions and High Average Unit Department Stddev\", \"category\": \"Course Catalog and Department Analysis\", \"desc\": \"List, for each department, either (a) the department's full name, the range and variance of the total units for degree-granting Mathematics department courses offered in the 2008 academic year along with the long course description for each course (with the reason 'Math 2008 Stats'), or (b) the department name, the average and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for subjects offered by that department (considering only subjects with more than 0 total units) where the average total units is greater than the overall average across all departments (with the reason 'High Avg Units'). Show the columns in the following order: department name, total units range, total units variance, average total units, standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of total units, long course description, and reason for inclusion. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_1766\", \"name\": \"Math Degree-Granting Course Level Counts with Min Units, Course Options, and Highest Term Average Library Enrollment\", \"category\": \"Course Catalog and Department Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each department name and course level where the course is degree granting, the total units are greater than 6, and the department is Mathematics (Course 18), provide the department name, course level, number of unique courses, minimum total units offered, school name, number of distinct course options available, and the highest average number of enrolled students in any term for courses offered by that department, considering only courses with more than 0 enrolled students and departments whose name is not null. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_2210\", \"name\": \"Math Subject Code School Ranks Matched with 2024 Catalog Offerings and Department Min Units\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Course Catalog Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each subject code in degree-granting departments where the department is Mathematics, and for subjects offered in the academic year 2024 that are also present in the CIS course catalog and are in the Mathematics department, show the subject code, subject code description, department name, school name, rank of the subject code within each school name group ordered by subject code, subject ID, subject number, subject short title, subject title, lecture units, lab units, total units, grade type, grade rule, the minimum total units value over each department code group, and the subject description from the CIS course catalog, ordered by school name, rank, and subject number. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_2335\", \"name\": \"Math Degree-Granting Course Level Counts with Catalog Unit Stddev and Unique Subject Codes\", \"category\": \"Course Catalog and Department Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each department name and course level, where the total number of enrolled students in offered subjects is greater than 10, and the department is Mathematics (Course 18), provide the number of unique courses, the minimum total units among those subjects that are degree-granting courses, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for Mathematics courses (considering only departments that offer more than five courses), and the number of unique subject codes for Mathematics in the SIS_SUBJECT_CODE table. List the department name, course level, number of unique courses, minimum total units, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of total units, and the number of unique subject codes, in that order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_2377\", \"name\": \"Math 2022 Unit Range-Variance with Offered-This-Year Subjects and Responsible Faculty Contact Windows\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Faculty Directory Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each department that is Mathematics (Course 18), provide the department's name, the range and variance of the total units for subjects offered by that department in the academic year 2022 and that are also listed in the CIS course catalog, and for all course subjects in the catalog where the department code is 18 (Mathematics), the department name is 'Mathematics', and the subject is offered this year, show the subject code, subject number, responsible faculty's full name, Moira list member, the average office phone number in a window of 2 preceding and 2 following rows grouped by the responsible faculty's last name and ordered by the subject code, and the email address of the responsible faculty. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3311\", \"name\": \"Status-U Library Subjects with Enrollment Matched with Department Offered-This-Year Unit Dispersion\", \"category\": \"Library Reserve and Course Catalog Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each course that has more than 0 enrolled students and a material status key of 'U', list the course number, course number description, number of enrolled students, reserve catalog key, and the dense rank over the material status key ordered by material status key, along with the department name, the range, variance, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units of courses offered by that department (considering only courses offered this year with non-null total units). Present the results ordered by course number and course number description. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3590\", \"name\": \"Union of Subject Code School Dense Ranks and 2012SU Cluster-S Subject Unit Row Numbers\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Course Catalog Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"Show, for each subject, the subject code, subject code description, department name, subject title, and the dense rank of each row partitioned by the school code and ordered by school code for subjects where the school code is not null and the subject title is not null; and for subjects offered in the 2012SU term with a cluster type of 'S', show the subject title from SUBJECT_OFFERED, the offer department name, the total units from SUBJECT_SUMMARY, and assign row numbers within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by the subject title. Indicate the source of each row as either 'Subq1' or 'Subq2'. List all results together, showing the columns: subject code, subject code description, department name, subject title, dense rank by school, offer department name, total units, row number window, and source, in that order, ordered by subject title. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_5279\", \"name\": \"2014JA Cross-Enrollment and Chemistry Subjects Listed as Offered in Academic Year Count\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Course Catalog Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"How many subjects offered in the 2014 January term by the Harvard Cross-Enrollment Program and the Chemistry department are listed in the course catalog as being offered in the academic year? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_538\", \"name\": \"Political Science 2022 Catalog Subjects Total Units Range and Variance per HASS Attribute with Form and Bulletin Descriptions\", \"category\": \"Course Catalog Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each HASS attribute, what is the range and variance of the total units for subjects offered in the 2022 academic year by the Political Science department, along with the HASS attribute's description as shown on the form and the description in the bulletin? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_104\", \"name\": \"Math 2022 Bulletin-Printed Subject Total Units Deviation from Department Average\", \"category\": \"Course Catalog and Department Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the academic year 2022 that are printed in the bulletin and belong to the Mathematics department (Course 18), show the subject title, department name, total units, and the difference between the total units of each subject and the average total units for Mathematics subjects in 2022. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_1471\", \"name\": \"Math 2024 12-Unit Subjects Ranked by School with Department Unit Dispersion and Communication Intensive Counts\", \"category\": \"Course Catalog and Department Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the academic year 2024 with a total of 12 units in the Mathematics department (Course 18), show the subject code, subject title, department name, school name, and the rank within each school name group ordered by subject code, but only include those subjects whose total units exceed the average total units for their respective school. Additionally, for the Mathematics department, also show the average, variance, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for subjects offered by that department (considering only subjects that are offered this year, are letter graded, and are in the Mathematics department), as well as the number of subjects that are Communication Intensive (i.e., have a non-null COMM_REQ_ATTRIBUTE), with these statistics included for each subject in the result. Present the columns in the following order: subject code, subject title, department name, school name, rank within school, average total units, total units variance, total units standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP), and number of Communication Intensive subjects. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_1758\", \"name\": \"Math 2024 12-Unit Subjects Row Numbers and Unit Deviations Matched with 2019FA TIP Course-Material Offerings\", \"category\": \"Course Catalog and Textbook Material Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the academic year 2024 with total units equal to 12 in the Mathematics department, show the department code, department name, subject code, subject number, subject title, total units, the row number within each department ordered by subject code, the deviation of each subject's total units from the average total units of all Mathematics subjects offered in 2024, the number of enrolled students, responsible faculty name, school name, and the dense rank over the department name ordered by department name for those subjects that also have course materials and were offered in the term '2019FA'. Sort the table by department name and subject title. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_1833\", \"name\": \"Math Letter-Graded Subject Rollup by Grade Type with Organization Room Area Stddev and DLC Name\", \"category\": \"Course Catalog and Facility Space Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each department and subject grade type where the subject is offered in the current academic year, is letter graded, and the department is Mathematics (Course 18), provide the number of subjects, the minimum total units, the school name, the department phone number, the organization name, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the areas of its rooms, and the department's DLC name, including subtotals for each department (the corresponding department field is 'SUBTOTAL') and a grand total across all departments (the corresponding department field is 'TOTAL'). Do not repeat the department if it is the same as the previous row. Only include organizations that have more than 5 rooms, are associated with a non-null DLC key, and are not the 'ADMISSIONS' department or the 'Political Science' department. Sort the table by department, grade type, and descending standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of room areas. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_2151\", \"name\": \"Degree-Granting Department 2022 Unit Average-Variance with Political Science HGN Lecture Unit Maximums\", \"category\": \"Course Catalog and Department Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each department that grants degrees (excluding the Biology department), provide the department name, the average and variance of the total units for subjects offered by that department in the 2022 academic year, and, if the department is Political Science, also include for each HGN code the maximum number of lecture units among all subjects in the course catalog and the subject title from the subject offered table for subjects offered in the year 2012 with more than 2 lecture units, as well as the number of enrolled students for those subjects. List the results ordered by the variance of total units in descending order, and for Political Science, by the maximum lecture units in descending order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_2158\", \"name\": \"Math 2022 TIP Subjects with Joint-Subject Flag and Letter-Graded Unit Range-Variance\", \"category\": \"Textbook Material and Subject Offering Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each subject offered in the 2022 academic year by a degree-granting department, specifically in the Department of Mathematics (Course 18) and excluding subjects offered by the Department of Physics, provide the subject ID, subject title, department name, the number of enrolled students, the total number of lecture units, and, for each subject, indicate whether it is also offered as a joint subject with another department. Additionally, show the range and variance of the total units for letter graded subjects offered this year in the Mathematics department. List the results in order of subject ID. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_2398\", \"name\": \"Department Course Counts with Fall-Only Non-Summer Subject Average TIP Enrollment\", \"category\": \"Course Catalog and Department Analysis\", \"desc\": \"Show the department names, the corresponding SIS subject code, subject code descriptions, graduate level, the total number of courses per department, and the average number of enrolled students for each subject in the department, considering only subjects that are offered in the fall term and are not offered in the summer term. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_2924\", \"name\": \"Engineering Degree-Granting Course Subjects Above Department Average Total Units\", \"category\": \"Course Catalog and Department Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For degree-granting courses in the School of Engineering, show the course description, department name, subject title, and the subject's grade type description, but only include those courses where the total units for the subject exceed the average total units for that department. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3236\", \"name\": \"Engineering Catalog Subjects Row Numbers Matched with 2017JA TIP Enrollment Windows\", \"category\": \"Course Catalog and Textbook Material Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered by departments in the School of Engineering that are also offered in the term '2017JA', show the subject title, total units, department full name, the row number within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by subject title, number of enrolled students, offering department name, department full name for the term, subject code, subject code description, and the minimum number of enrolled students over each subject code group, ordered by subject title and subject code. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3668\", \"name\": \"Engineering Catalog Subjects Row Numbers Matched with TIP Material Detail Enrollment Windows\", \"category\": \"Course Catalog and Textbook Material Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered by departments in the School of Engineering, show the subject title, total units, department full name, and assign row numbers within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by subject title. Additionally, for each matching course material detail, provide the material status key, term code, subject ID, ISBN, material key, the course number description, the offering department name, and the maximum number of enrolled students for each row considering the current row and the next 2 rows ordered by material key. The results should include the subject title, total units, department full name, window row number, material status key, term code, subject ID, ISBN, material key, course number description, offering department name, and the maximum number of enrolled students, in that order, for subjects and course materials where the subject title and department code match between the two datasets. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_4602\", \"name\": \"Engineering Subjects with Unique Course Material Counts and TIP Material Detail Enrollment Windows\", \"category\": \"Course Catalog and Textbook Material Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"Show the department full names, subject titles, total units, and the number of unique course materials per subject for subjects offered by departments in the School of Engineering. For each subject, also provide the material status key, term code, subject ID, ISBN, material key, course number description, offering department name, and the maximum number of enrolled students for each row considering the current row and the next 2 rows ordered by material key, where the subject title and department code match between the subject and course material datasets. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_5150\", \"name\": \"Count of Spring Math Catalog Subjects with 6+ Units Taught by Faculty with Enrolled Subject Offerings\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Enrollment Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"How many subjects in the course catalog are offered in the spring term, have a total of at least 6 units, are taught by faculty who are responsible for at least one subject with more than 0 enrolled students according to the subject offered summary, and are in the Mathematics department (Course 18)? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_1965\", \"name\": \"2017JA Chemistry TIP Subjects with Course Materials Enrollment Windows and Per-Faculty Max Enrollment\", \"category\": \"Textbook Material and Enrollment Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the term '2017JA' by the Chemistry department (Course 5) that have course materials, show the subject title, the number of enrolled students, the responsible faculty name, the offering department name, the department full name, the school name, the minimum number of enrolled students in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the department code, the subject code, the subject code description, the minimum number of enrolled students over each subject code group ordered by subject code, and the maximum number of enrolled students for each responsible faculty across all their Chemistry subjects in that term. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_1221\", \"name\": \"2014FA Chemistry Library Subjects Windowed Enrollment with Department Reserve Enrollment Average and Normalized Ratio\", \"category\": \"Library Reserve and Textbook Material Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the term '2014FA' by the Chemistry department, show the subject title from the library, the number of enrolled students in the library subject, the responsible faculty name from the TIP subject, the offer department name from the TIP subject, and the minimum number of enrolled students in the library subject within a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the TIP subject's responsible faculty MIT ID, as well as the average and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the number of enrolled students in courses with at least one reserved library material and a material status of 'U' offered by either the Chemistry or Biology department, and calculate the normalized enrollment ratio (the number of enrolled students in the library subject divided by the average enrollment for the department, rounded to two decimal places). List the results in descending order of normalized enrollment ratio.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3356\", \"name\": \"Top 10 Reserved-Material Subjects in 2009SP with Degree-Granting Department Enrollment Variance and Stddev\", \"category\": \"Library Reserve and Enrollment Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For the top 10 subject titles by the number of reserved library materials for subjects offered in the term '2009SP', what are the subject title, the offering department name, the variance and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the number of enrolled students in subjects offered by that department (considering only departments that grant degrees and subjects with a non-null subject code description), and the count of reserved materials? Please provide the subject title, the offering department name, the variance, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP), and the count of reserved materials, in that order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3868\", \"name\": \"Above-Average Engineering Department Enrollments with Status-U Reserve Material and Textbook Details\", \"category\": \"Library Reserve and Enrollment Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each department in the School of Engineering where the total number of students enrolled in courses offered by that department is greater than the average total enrollment across all Engineering departments (and the total enrollment is greater than 50), show the department name and total enrollment, and for each such department, show the library reserve material details with material status key equal to 'U', including the library course instructor key, library reserve catalog key, term code, subject ID, the tip material key, tip material status key, tip ISBN, the subject title, the minimum tip material status key in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the number of enrolled students, as well as the responsible faculty name and the offer department name, for materials offered by that department. The columns should be: department name, total enrollment, library course instructor key, library reserve catalog key, term code, subject ID, tip material key, tip material status key, tip ISBN, subject title, windowed minimum tip material status key, responsible faculty name, and offer department name. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_4458\", \"name\": \"2009SP Status-U Reserve Materials Windowed Faculty Row Numbers with EECS Course Student Directory Details\", \"category\": \"Library Reserve and Student Directory Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each library reserve material detail with material status key 'U' and term code '2009SP', show the course instructor key, reserve catalog key, subject offered key, the responsible faculty name, and the row number within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by the responsible faculty name from the associated subject offered, and for each matching course in the \\\"Electrical Eng & Computer Sci\\\" department, show the course description, course level, the full name and email address of students enrolled, and the row number within each course level group ordered by the student's last name. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_1165\", \"name\": \"Library-TIP Matched Subjects by Faculty or Enrollment with Degree-Granting Graduate Department Enrollment Dispersion\", \"category\": \"Library Reserve and Textbook Material Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each subject where the responsible faculty MIT ID in the library subject offered table is 928034000 or the number of enrolled students in the tip subject offered table is greater than 5, and where the offer department name in the tip subject offered table is either 'Chemistry' or 'Biology', show the subject title from the library subject offered table, the offer department name from the tip subject offered table, the term code from both tables, the number of enrolled students from both tables, and the minimum number of enrolled students in the tip subject offered table over each master subject ID group. Additionally, for the department offering the subject, show the department name, the range of enrolled students, and the variance of enrolled students in the subjects offered by that department, considering only departments that grant degrees, courses that are at the graduate level, and excluding the Biology department. Present the results ordered by subject title and department name. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_2591\", \"name\": \"2014FA Enrolled Library Subjects with TIP Material Status and 3-Row Min Total Units\", \"category\": \"Library Reserve and Textbook Material Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For all subjects in the 2014FA term with at least one enrolled student, show the subject title, offering department name, responsible faculty name, the TIP material status key, the total number of units, and the minimum total number of units in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the course number, along with the cluster type description and the HGN code description for each subject. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_4812\", \"name\": \"Top 10 Degree-Granting Department Subject Code and Course Number Combinations by Unique Library Subject Count\", \"category\": \"Library Reserve and Course Catalog Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"From the top 10 combinations of department name, subject code, and course number (where the department is degree granting and the number of enrolled students in the subject summary is greater than 2) with the highest number of unique library subjects offered, display the department name, subject code, number of subject codes, minimum department budget code, course number, number of unique library subjects offered, minimum total units, the subject title with the most enrolled students for that course, and the corresponding number of enrolled students. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_1212\", \"name\": \"Math Department Subject Unit Average-Stddev with Graduate Student Count and Latest Load Date\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Student Directory Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For the Mathematics department (Course 18), provide the department name, the average and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for subjects offered by that department (considering only subjects with more than 0 total units and at least 1 enrolled student), the number of graduate students in the department, and the most recent warehouse load date for those students, considering only departments that are degree granting and students whose year is 'G'. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_1350\", \"name\": \"Degree-Granting Department TIP Enrollment Statistics with School Rollups and Math Peter Student Budget Code Windows\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Student Directory Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each department and school, provide the department name, school name, the average, range, and variance of the number of enrolled students in subjects offered by that department, and the total enrolled students, considering only departments that grant degrees and subjects with at least one enrolled student. Additionally, for each school, include a grand total for all departments in that school in the format of (null department name, school name, nulls for statistics, and total enrolled students). For students whose first name is 'Peter' and who are in the Mathematics department, also show their last name, email address, student year, and the minimum department budget code in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the student's full name, as well as the department full name and department last activity date. The results include all these columns in the following order: department name, school name, average enrolled students, range of enrolled students, variance of enrolled students, total enrolled students, last name, email address, student year, windowed minimum department budget code, department full name, and department last activity date. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_1474\", \"name\": \"Top 10 Engineering Degree-Granting Department Subject Counts with Kevin EECS Student Course Windows\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Student Directory Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For the top 10 degree-granting departments (excluding 'Political Science' and Course 17) that have offered at least one subject in the 'Engineering' school, list the department name, school name, subject code description, the total number of subjects they offered, and the average number of enrolled students per subject, and for each such department, show the full names, email addresses, student years, department full names, course descriptions, course levels, the minimum course level in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the student's last name, and the corresponding subject code and subject code description for each course taken by students named 'Kevin' in 'Electrical Eng & Computer Sci' (Course 6). Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_1983\", \"name\": \"EECS Students Windowed Admin Department Phone Averages with Engineering Subject Load Categories\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Student Directory Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For students whose department is '6' and whose department name is 'Electrical Eng & Computer Sci', show their first name, last name, department name, student year, the corresponding department's full name, the administrative department name, and the average department phone number in a window of 2 preceding and 2 following rows grouped by the administrative department name and ordered by the student's first name. Additionally, for each subject offered in the 'Engineering' school with total units greater than 0 and only for subjects in the 'Electrical Eng & Computer Sci' department (Course 6), where the student's department matches the subject's offer department code, show the subject title, total units, subject department name, course description, and the dense rank over the offer department code ordered by offer department code. Finally, for each such subject, include the corresponding department's school name and whether the total units are 'HIGH_LOAD' (at least 12), 'LOW_LOAD' (at most 6), or 'MEDIUM_LOAD' (otherwise). Present the columns in the following order: first name, last name, department name, student year, department full name, administrative department name, average department phone number (windowed), subject title, total units, subject department name, course description, dense rank (windowed), department school name, and subject load category. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_2240\", \"name\": \"EECS Engineering Subject Max Units and Distinct Student Year Counts per Offer Department\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Student Directory Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each subject offered in the 'Engineering' school with total units greater than 0 and only for subjects in the 'Electrical Eng & Computer Sci' department (Course 6), show the subject title, total units, department name, course description, and dense rank over the offer department code ordered by offer department code, along with the first name, last name, department name, student year, corresponding department's full name, administrative department name, and the average department phone number in a window of 2 preceding and 2 following rows grouped by the administrative department name and ordered by the student's first name, for students whose department is '6' and whose department name is 'Electrical Eng & Computer Sci', where the subject's offer department code matches the student's department. Then, for each offer department code, provide the maximum total units among these subjects and the count of distinct student years among the matched students. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3237\", \"name\": \"2021 Engineering Degree-Granting Department Subject Counts with Active Graduate Student Office Totals\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Student Directory Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each department that is degree-granting and offered at least one subject in the School of Engineering in 2021, provide the department code, department name, department full name, the number of subjects offered, the total number of enrolled students in those subjects, and the total number of active graduate students with an office location assigned in that department. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3969\", \"name\": \"2017JA Subject Enrollment Windows Matched with Above-Average-Last-Name EECS Student Row Numbers\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Student Directory Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the term '2017JA', and for students in the \\\"Electrical Eng & Computer Sci\\\" department whose last name is alphabetically after the average last name (in terms of ASCII value) within their course level group, show the subject title, number of enrolled students, offering department name, department full name, subject code, subject code description, the minimum number of enrolled students over each subject code group, the school name, department phone number, the student's full name, email address, department name, course description, course level, and the student's row number within their course level group ordered by last name. Order the results by subject code, course level, and student row number within course level. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_1954\", \"name\": \"2019FA Chemistry TIP Subjects Windowed Min Enrollment with Department Subject Code Statistics\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Course Catalog Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the term '2019FA' with more than 0 enrolled students, offered by the Chemistry department (Course 5), and only including courses that have course materials, show the subject title, offering department name, school name, department full name, and the minimum number of enrolled students in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the department name. Additionally, for the same department, provide the department name, the average and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the number of unique subject codes associated with its courses that are offered by degree-granting departments, but only include departments other than 'Mathematics' (Course 18). Also, for each of these departments, show the total number of courses offered by the department in the '2019FA' term that have at least one enrolled student and have course materials. Present the subject title, offering department name, school name, department full name, windowed minimum enrolled students, department name, average number of unique subject codes, standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of unique subject codes, and the total number of such courses, in that order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_4208\", \"name\": \"2016SP Engineering School Subject Row Numbers Matched with 2017JA TIP Subject Enrollment Windows\", \"category\": \"Enrollment and Subject Offering Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the term '2016SP' with a school code of 'E', and for subjects offered in the term '2017JA', show the subject title, department name, course description, the number of enrolled students in 2016SP, the row number within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by subject title, the number of enrolled students in 2017JA, the offering department name, department full name, subject code, subject code description, the minimum number of enrolled students over each subject code group in 2017JA, the school name, and the department phone number. Order the results by subject title and subject code. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_2639\", \"name\": \"2016SP Engineering School Subjects Total Units Minus Lecture Units\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Course Catalog Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the term '2016SP' with a school code of 'E', show the subject title, department name, course description, and the difference between the total units and lecture units for each subject. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3273\", \"name\": \"Engineering 12-Unit Courses Row Numbers with Subject Dense Ranks by Total Units\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Course Catalog Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For courses in the School of Engineering with a total of 12 units, display the course number, course description, subject title, total units, offering department name, the row number of the course within its offering department ordered by course number, and the dense rank of the subject (considering the current and 2 preceding rows ordered by total units) if available. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3794\", \"name\": \"2019FA TIP Subject Enrollment Windows Matched with Engineering 12-Unit Course Row Numbers\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Enrollment Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the term '2019FA' with more than 0 enrolled students, and for courses in the 'Engineering' school with a total of 12 units, show the subject title, offer department name, department full name, number of enrolled students, the average number of enrolled students in a window of 2 preceding and 2 following rows grouped by the school code, the course number, course description, course subject title, total units, course offering department name, and the row number of the course within each offering department ordered by course number, for cases where the subject and course are from the same offering department. Order the results by subject title and course number. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_4234\", \"name\": \"2016SP Degree-Granting Department Subject Rollups Matched with Top-5 Engineering 12-Unit Course Departments\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Course Catalog Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each department that grants degrees and offered subjects in the term '2016SP', and is also among the top 5 offering departments in the 'Engineering' school with the most 12-unit courses, list the department code, department name, the number of subjects offered, the total units for those subjects, the offering department name, the number of qualifying 12-unit courses, and the course number and description of the most recently added 12-unit course in each department. For each department, also include a grand total row for the number of subjects and total units in the format (department code, null, total subjects, total units, ...). Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_4490\", \"name\": \"Degree-Granting Subject Code Description Status Rollup by School with 2016SP Engineering Subject Row Numbers\", \"category\": \"Course Catalog and Subject Offering Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each subject code where the department is degree granting, show the subject code, subject code description, department name, school name, the number of subject codes per school name, and whether the subject code description is present ('Has Description') or missing ('No Description'). For each school name, include a grand total for all subject codes in the format of (null, null, null, school name, null, total subject codes). Additionally, for subjects offered in the term '2016SP' with a school code of 'E', show the subject title, course description, the offering department name, and assign row numbers within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by subject title. Present all columns in the following order: subject code, subject code description, department name, school name, description status, total subject codes, subject title, course description, offering department name, and window column. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_1689\", \"name\": \"School Highest Department Average TIP Enrollment with 2019FA Chemistry Course-Material Subject Dense Ranks\", \"category\": \"Enrollment and Subject Offering Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each school, what is the school name and the highest average number of enrolled students per department (among its degree-granting departments, excluding Chemistry, and only considering subjects with at least one enrolled student), and for each subject offered by the Chemistry department in the 2019FA term that has course materials, what is the subject title, the dense rank of the subject considering the current and 2 preceding rows ordered by the number of enrolled students descending, the full name of the offering department, and the school name of the Chemistry department? List the school name and highest average enrolled students per department first, followed by the Chemistry subject title, dense rank, department full name, and Chemistry school name. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3644\", \"name\": \"2012SU 1-Unit Subject Row Numbers per Department with Department Offered Summary Unit Average-Stddev\", \"category\": \"Enrollment and Subject Offering Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the 2012SU term with a total of 1 unit, show the subject title from the summary, the course number from the offered table, the subject title from the offered summary, the department name from the summary, the offer department name from the offered summary, the row number within each department name group ordered by subject title from the summary, and for each department, also provide the average and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for subjects offered by that department (considering only subjects with more than 0 total units and at least 1 enrolled student). List the results ordered by department name and row number. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_4527\", \"name\": \"2021 Engineering Degree-Granting Department Enrollment Dispersion with Above-Average Subject Details\", \"category\": \"Enrollment and Subject Offering Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each department that is degree-granting and offered at least one subject in the School of Engineering in 2021, provide the department code, department name, department full name, the number of subjects offered, the total number of enrolled students in those subjects, the variance and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the number of enrolled students in subjects offered by that department (considering only subjects with a non-null subject code description), and, for each subject in 2021 offered by these departments in the School of Engineering, list the subject id, subject title, and the number of enrolled students, but only include subjects where the number of enrolled students exceeds the average enrollment for that department in 2021. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_4640\", \"name\": \"2017JA Subject Enrollment Windows with Department Enrollment Coefficient of Variation and School Code\", \"category\": \"Enrollment and Subject Offering Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each subject offered in the term '2017JA', what is the subject title, the number of enrolled students, the responsible faculty name, the offering department name, the department full name, the school name, the