ED | SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY | COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Granularity | one row per subject **section** per term (retrieved desc) | one row per **subject** per term (retrieved desc) | one row per subject offering per term/academic year (retrieved desc) |\n| Enrollment measure | NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS, SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER, SECTION_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER (columns) | NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS, SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER (columns) | **none** (column list verified) |\n| Meeting place / room link | MEET_PLACE \"Meeting place of the section\" (columns) | **none** (column list verified) | MEET_PLACE \"stores the FCLT room key and joins to FCLT_ROOMS.FCLT_ROOM_KEY\" (columns) |\n| Term filter | TERM_CODE | TERM_CODE | TERM_CODE / EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE |\n| Department | OFFER_DEPT_CODE/OFFER_DEPT_NAME | OFFER_DEPT_CODE/OFFER_DEPT_NAME | DEPARTMENT_CODE/DEPARTMENT_NAME |\n| Fan-out risk | section rows multiply per subject | none at subject level | section flags also present |\n\n**3b. Task-Requirement Fitness:**\n- Requirement \"number of students enrolled in its offered subjects\" (STDDEV): SUBJECT_OFFERED **SUPPORTED** (NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS; dw_2958 precedent computes STDDEV(NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) from SUBJECT_OFFERED per department); SUMMARY **SUPPORTED**; CATALOG **NOT-SUPPORTED** (no enrollment column).\n- Requirement \"rooms used for subjects offered by that department\" (AVG/VARIANCE/STDDEV of AREA, AREA > 100): SUBJECT_OFFERED **SUPPORTED** (has MEET_PLACE; same value domain as catalog MEET_PLACE per MEET_PLACE column descriptions); SUMMARY **NOT-SUPPORTED** (no MEET_PLACE); CATALOG **SUPPORTED** (documented FCLT_ROOM_KEY join, dw_4061 precedent).\n- Requirement \"more than 10 subjects offered in the 2022FA term\" (HAVING): all three **SUPPORTED** via TERM_CODE + GROUP BY dept + HAVING COUNT (dw_3985/dw_1049 precedents).\n- Requirement \"department name\" output: all **SUPPORTED** (OFFER_DEPT_NAME / DEPARTMENT_NAME; column_concept_department_name confirms both conventions share the academic value domain).\n- Only **SUBJECT_OFFERED** satisfies all requirements in a single table + FCLT_ROOMS join.\n\n**3c. Wording-to-Field Anchoring:**\n- \"number of students enrolled\" → lexically matches NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS (\"Number of students enrolled…\") per column_concept_enrollment_measures; SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER is the \"official registrar enrollment\" wording — excluded.\n- \"rooms … area\" → FCLT_ROOMS.AREA (\"Room area in square meters; used in area statistics (average, range, variance)\") — exact match; SPACE_DETAIL square footage and building assignable area excluded (different objects/units per concept_room_space_inventory).\n- \"2022FA term\" → TERM_CODE = '2022FA' (column_concept_term_code: YYYYTT format, 'FA' = Fall).\n- \"Course 8\" → department code '8' (precedents dw_2461 \"Chemistry department (Course 5)\" and dw_1049 \"Mathematics (Course 18)\" anchor \"Course N\" to DEPARTMENT_CODE/OFFER_DEPT_CODE = 'N').\n- \"rooms used for subjects offered\" → MEET_PLACE = FCLT_ROOM_KEY (dw_4061 precedent `JOIN FCLT_ROOMS fr ON cso.MEET_PLACE = fr.FCLT_ROOM_KEY`).\n\n**3d. Precedent Usage Evidence:**\n- STDDEV of NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS per department: 2 precedents on SUBJECT_OFFERED-family tables (dw_2958 on SUBJECT_OFFERED; dw_4527/dw_3356 on TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED — TIP lacks MEET_PLACE and term-2022FA room linkage).\n- MEET_PLACE→FCLT_ROOMS.FCLT_ROOM_KEY join: 1 precedent (dw_4061, on COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED).\n- \"more than N subjects offered in term\" as HAVING COUNT: 2 precedents (dw_3985 `HAVING COUNT(*) > 5`; dw_1049 `HAVING COUNT(*) > 5`).\n- STDDEV(AREA) of rooms: dw_1833, dw_1465 (organization-assigned rooms — different join path, not \"rooms used for subjects\").\n\n### 4. Business Usage\n\n- **SUBJECT_OFFERED**: consumed by 142 metrics (enrollment windows, department dispersion, term filters); the registrar's actual section record — serves \"what was actually taught, where, and how many students\" questions.\n- **FCLT_ROOMS**: consumed by 16 metrics for room-area statistics (dw_4061, dw_1190, dw_1833, dw_1488…); the canonical room inventory with AREA in m².\n- **SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY**: subject-level enrollment reporting (dw_4527); no facility linkage.\n- **COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED**: catalog attribute questions and the documented MEET_PLACE→FCLT_ROOMS bridge (dw_4061); no enrollment.\n- **SIS_DEPARTMENT**: department name/full name/school/degree-granting enrichment in dozens of metrics.\n\n### 5. Coverage Checklist\n\nAll Phase 1 survivors investigated: SUBJECT_OFFERED, SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY, COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED, FCLT_ROOMS, SIS_DEPARTMENT (semantic_get + query_neighbors + metrics_by_table for SUBJECT_OFFERED/FCLT_ROOMS); metrics dw_4061, dw_1833, dw_4640, dw_1049, dw_2461, dw_2958, dw_4527, dw_3356, dw_3985 (semantic_get full SQL); concepts concept_subject_offering_facts, concept_room_space_inventory, concept_department_dimension and column concepts enrollment_measures, department_name, term_code, subject_id, building_room, office_location, assignable_area, access_level, facility_organization_key, space_unit_key, master_subject_id (semantic_search desc + targeted search). Low-score/unrelated entities (IAP, Moira, TIP-material-only, CIP, time-dimension tables) were screened out in Phase 1 as not matching any task keyword except term code, which is covered. **Note: mysql_query was attempted 5 times and failed every time with error 1045 (Access denied for user 'root'@'localhost') — data-level verification was impossible; all claims above are grounded in retrieved definitions and precedent SQL.**\n\n### 6. Recommendation\n\n**6a. Tables/columns:** SUBJECT_OFFERED (measure `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS`; keys `TERM_CODE='2022FA'`, `OFFER_DEPT_CODE='8'`; output `OFFER_DEPT_NAME`; join key `MEET_PLACE`; HAVING key `SUBJECT_ID`) ⋈ FCLT_ROOMS (`FCLT_ROOM_KEY`, measure `AREA`).\n\n**6b. SQL approach:** single flat join `SUBJECT_OFFERED.MEET_PLACE = FCLT_ROOMS.FCLT_ROOM_KEY` (dw_4061 precedent), WHERE term/dept/AREA>100, GROUP BY department name, HAVING COUNT(SUBJECT_ID) > 10 (dw_3985/dw_1049 precedent), bare STDDEV()/VARIANCE()/AVG(), no rounding. SELECT exactly 5 columns in asked order.\n\n**6c. Reasons:** *Data* — SUBJECT_OFFERED is the only candidate physically carrying both an enrollment column and a meeting-place column (verified column lists); FCLT_ROOMS.AREA is the documented room-area measure. *Semantic-network* — FCLT_ROOMS' documented incoming MEET_PLACE join and dw_4061's `MEET_PLACE = FCLT_ROOM_KEY` lineage; dw_2958's STDDEV(NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS)-per-department lineage on SUBJECT_OFFERED. *Business* — \"Course 8\" anchoring, \"more than N subjects offered in term\" HAVING pattern, and \"STDDEV only, never STDDEV_POP\" phrasing all match existing metric precedents.\n\n**6d. Caveat:** DB verification was blocked by the auth error; if MEET_PLACE in SUBJECT_OFFERED were empty for 2022FA, the fallback would be routing rooms through COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED — but the section-level MEET_PLACE is the direct registrar record of where each offered section met, matching \"rooms used for subjects offered\".\n\n",
